---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../lib/brand.mjs';
import { getSite, quality as q } from '../lib/site.mjs';
const s = getSite();
const conservative = s.feeRule === 'conservative';
const downloads = s.planned.find((p) => p.type === 'fee-comparison').eligible;
// Rule changes are logged here with a date (PRD section 6, item 6).
const changes = [
  { date: '2026-11-12', text: 'First published rules: ordering, freshness limits, page thresholds and the fee comparison scope described on this page.' },
  { date: '2026-11-14', text: 'Fee rows now say how they were checked. Rows from a network-wide pricing page or with unconfirmed plan labels are shown with a note and are not counted toward the thresholds. Facts count toward indexed pages only when the source\'s terms have been reviewed.' }
];
---
<Base title="Methodology: how we collect, check and rank" description="Where the facts come from, how companies are ordered, how old a fact can be, and which pages exist only when there is enough verified data." pageType="methodology" crumbs={[{ name: 'Methodology' }]}>
  <h1>Methodology</h1>
  <p class="lede">How facts get into this directory, how we order companies and when a page is allowed to exist.</p>

  <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page"><ol><li><a href="#read">How to read this site</a>: where facts come from and what each label means</li><li><a href="#rules">Rules and change log</a>: how companies are ordered, how old a fact can be, when a page exists</li></ol></nav>

  <h2 id="read">How to read this site</h2>
  <h3>What we list</h3>
  <p>We list a company only after reading its own website. Companies seen only on a third-party directory or in a search result are not published. We collect facts (fees, services, service areas, license notes, public business contact details), not descriptions or images.</p>

  <h3>Sources and dates</h3>
  <p>Every fact carries a source, the date we captured it and the date we last read it, shown next to the fact. Our rule is to check a source's terms and robots.txt before collecting from it automatically. An unknown fact stays unknown: it shows as &ldquo;Not published&rdquo; (we recorded that the company does not state it) or &ldquo;Not recorded&rdquo; (we have no record of looking). We never fill a gap with a guess or with a figure from a third-party roundup.</p>

  <h3>How a fee was checked</h3>
  <p>Each fee row says how it was checked. &ldquo;Read from the company's website by our tool&rdquo; means an automated tool read the value from the company's own page on the date shown. It is not a quote, and fees change, so confirm with the company. &ldquo;Checked by a person&rdquo; means a person compared the value with the live page. We do not call a fee &ldquo;verified&rdquo; in either case. We do not describe a license as verified unless we checked an official record; none of our sources for that are available yet, so license notes read &ldquo;stated by company, not verified&rdquo;.</p>
  <p>We use a source for pages that can be indexed only after its terms of service have been reviewed and recorded. Company pages with too little reviewed data are not published.</p>

  <h3>Fee comparison scope</h3>
  <p>The fee comparison and fee guides use only fees a company publishes on its own website, labelled &ldquo;companies we reviewed, not a market average&rdquo;. They are not a survey. Ranges and plans are shown as published and are never averaged. A rent estimate uses an example rent and is an illustration, not a quote.</p>
  {conservative && <p>A company's fees are included only if its own website also states a Columbus-area service area. Fees from a company with no stated service area are not shown until it states one.</p>}

  {downloads && <><h3>Use the data</h3><p>The published fee rows are available as <a href="/fees-data/columbus-pm-fees.csv">CSV</a> and <a href="/fees-data/columbus-pm-fees.json">JSON</a>, with the source page and dates for every figure. It lists companies we reviewed, not a market average. Please cite &ldquo;{SITE_NAME} fee data, as of {s.today}&rdquo;.</p></>}

  <h3>License notes</h3>
  <p>Ohio has no separate property manager license. A company's license note shows what its own site says or, when we have checked it, what the state record shows. A company-stated license is labelled &ldquo;stated by company, not verified&rdquo;.</p>

  <h3>Corrections</h3>
  <p>Companies can correct or remove a listing for free on <a href="/corrections/">the correction page</a>. A correction is published when there is a public source for it.</p>


  <h2 id="rules">Rules and change log</h2>
  <h3>How we order companies</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Relevance to the page: serves this city or property type.</li>
    <li>Data completeness: how many of six fact groups are sourced and current (license, fees, service areas, services, property types, contact).</li>
    <li>Name, A to Z.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Payment, claiming a listing, company size, any business relationship with this site and the amount of a fee are never inputs. A company that does not publish fees is still listed.</p>

  <h3>How old a fact can be</h3>
  <p>A fact last read more than {q.freshness.displayFlagDays} days ago is flagged with its age. A fact more than {q.freshness.dropDays} days old is left out of fee comparisons and completeness until we re-check it.</p>

  <h3>When a page exists</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Company page: indexed by search engines only with at least {q.company.minFactGroups} sourced fact groups and fees from a company's own site or a license checked against the state record. Otherwise it is listed but marked not for indexing.</li>
    <li>City page: indexed with at least {q.city.indexMinCompanies} indexable companies, at least {q.city.indexMinCompaniesWithFees} with published fees we have read.</li>
    <li>Property-type page: at least {q.propertyType.indexMinCompanies} indexable companies with a sourced fact for that type.</li>
    <li>Fee comparison: at least {q.feeComparison.minCompanies} companies with published fees we have read. Each fee guide: at least {q.feeGuide.minCompaniesPerFeeType} companies publishing that fee.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Change log</h3>
  <ul>{changes.map((c) => <li><time datetime={c.date}>{c.date}</time>: {c.text}</li>)}</ul>
</Base>
